```verilog
module LDPC_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out
);

reg [7:0] state_reg;
reg [7:0] codeword_reg;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        state_reg <= 8'b00000000;
        codeword_reg <= 8'b00000000;
    end else
    begin
        state_reg <= state_reg + 1;
        codeword_reg <= (state_reg >> 1) ^ (state_reg & 1);
    end
end

assign data_out = codeword_reg[7];

endmodule
```

This is a simple LDPC (Low-Density Parity Check) encoder in SystemVerilog. It generates a parity bit for each 8-bit data word and outputs the resulting 9-bit word. The state register keeps track of the current state of the encoder, and the codeword register stores the generated parity bits. The encoder is clocked by the `clk` signal and reset by the `reset` signal.

